{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35"],
      "pins": ["U22.4", "U15.2", "U15.4", "U35.2"],
      "nets": ["LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV"],
      "observed": "On the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet the three open-drain sink buffers U22, U15 and U35 are daisy-chained, but the intermediate chain nodes are all given the identical global label 'LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV': U22 output (pin 4), U15 input (pin 2), U15 output (pin 4) and U35 input (pin 2) carry the same net name. This merges the node between U22 and U15 with the node between U15 and U35, so U15's input is shorted to its own output and U35 reads U22's output directly, bypassing U15.",
      "expected": "The specification states U15/U22/U35 are '/OE-controlled sinks' for ESTOP_SINK1/ESTOP_SINK2/ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL that must each be able to assert the e-stop chain (and the on-sheet changelog requires 'indicator lights for each branch' / a 'local motherboard branch'). For that, each buffer's input must be tied low (GND, as U22's pin 2 correctly is) or the chain nodes must be distinct nets so that asserting ESTOP_SINK2 actually pulls the chain low.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config': U22 pin4 -> wire -> U15 pin2, all labelled 'LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV'; U15 pin4 -> U35 pin2, also labelled 'LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV' (three identical top labels above D29/D28/D8)."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "'U15, U22, U35, U36 (SN74LVC1G07) wired as /OE gates on ESTOP_SINK1/ESTOP_SINK2/ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL ... feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ESTOP_SINK2 branch is non-functional: because U15's input is shorted to its output, enabling/disabling U15 via ESTOP_SINK2 cannot pull the e-stop chain low. Disconnecting the cable on that branch (e.g. CAN Interface A) will fail to trigger the e-stop, a safety regression.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The e-stop sink chain on the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet reuses the single net label 'LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV' on multiple distinct chain nodes, shorting U15's input to its output and bypassing it; this disables the ESTOP_SINK2 branch, contradicting the spec's three independent sink branches and the per-branch indicator intent. Other documented oddities (USB ideal-diode path, GLOBAL_EN sequencing, CAN LED polarity) are pre-existing known issues and were not reported."
}

